e back!"}\tg[Simon]Great, only no one has asked you to introduce me or tell them about my life.\nY they already know me, damn it."8\tg[Haya]Ah, I'm sorry\..\..\..\nExcuse me\..\..\.."S\tg[Owen]Take it easy, Professor.\nFrom my own experience, you get used to it."0\tg[Owen]More or less\..\..\..\nHa, ha, ha."@\tg[Simon]Okay, that's enough.\nLet's get down to business."r\tg[Simon]I have analyzed the code of Metis Corp.'s Realidea System and found something extremely suspicious."�\tg[Simon]As expected,\..\..\..\nthe system is designed so that if there is no initial link between trainer and Pokémon, a false one is created to access its functions."�\tg[Simon]And then, as Teresa said, the System itself will undo those false links after a certain period of time.\nSo far so good, I suppose."�\tg[Simon]The problem is a certain piece of code that doesn't make sense to be there.\nIt's messy and incomplete, but it's nothing to ignore."�\tg[Simon]Its function is to transfer the links registered by other trainers with their Pokémon to a single user.\nIn other words\..\..\.."�\tg[Simon]Such a user could link to all Pokémon of trainers in the region by completely removing the link to their original owners, fake or not."s\tg[Owen]Am I getting this right?\nAre you saying that they want to take over all the Pokémon in the region?!"H\tg[Owen]Then\..\..\..!\nTeresa and Jeremiah have been lying to us!"�\tg[Owen]They are the only ones who developed Metis Corp.'s Realidea System, right?\nThere's no way they could have done something like that unintentionally!"q\tg[Owen]But it's still not certain that they're going to use that code, right?\nAnd it's not even complete."}\tg[Simon]Yes, indeed\..\..\..\nbut unfortunately I have evidence that they may indeed plan to finish it and execute it."�\tg[Simon]To carry out something like this, the system not only needs a large amount of energy.\nit must also be extremely powerful."�\tg[Simon]On the one hand, it was already suspicious that they needed so much energy from the region to the point of resorting to a Celesteela in Jade City.\nIt's too massive an amount."x\tg[Simon]And on an additional note,\..\..\..\NI have found search records for a certain Pokémon known as Manaphy."A\tg[Haya]Oh, Manaphy!\nI know something about that Pokémon!"k\tg[Haya]It has the ability to bond with any other Pokémon it wants, right?\nThat's why it's special."W\tg[Simon]I hadn't gotten around to asking you\nbut thank you for the information."�\tg[Simon]They want Manaphy to extract its ability to establish links and introduce it into the Realidea System.\nWith this and if they manage to finish the code, the System could pose a threat to all Pokémon and trainers in the region."}\tg[Owen]Then we have to find Manaphy before they do at all costs!\nThat's why we're here with Professor Haya, isn't it?"<\tg[Simon]Indeed\nMiss Haya, where can we find Manaphy?"\tg[Haya]Ah.\nNo idea."M\tg[Simon]What do you mean, no idea?\nBut weren't you studying Pokémon?"|\tg[Haya]What did you say?\nHow am I supposed to know the whereabouts of a mystical Pokémon that could be anywhere!!!?"s\tg[Haya]I know it's an aquatic Pokémon so I'm guessing it's somewhere with water!\nAt sea, probably\..\..\.."�\tg[Haya]But if anyone can know anything about its precise location, then you should ask in Florita Village.\nThe ancestors of its inhabitants used to have links to mystical Pokémon."4\tg[Simon]That's enough.\nLet's go, \PN y Owen!"j\tg[Simon]I'm going to continue researching the code.\n You have to find Manaphy and stop Metis Corp."\tg[Owen]To get to Florita Town we have to go through Amberino Town and cross Route 13, right?\nI'm going there right now!"[\tg[Simon]And I'm going back to the Academy.\nI'll be there if you need anything, \PN."/\tg[Haya]Ah, Simon!\nHave you seen Elliot?"C\tg[Haya]He's grown a lot!\nI'm sure he'd be happy too\..\.\.."\tg[Simon]No!\nShut up!"A\tg[Haya]A-ah!\nI didn't say anything wrong, did I\..\..\..?")I think I should help t