e Jade City Gym Leader.\nHaving seen the battle against your rival, I'm sure you'll be quite a challenge!"�A long time ago a meteorite fell in the bamboo forest to the west of the town.\nApparently a Pokémon was traveling in it and it got buried."�It's been asleep for a long time and no one knows how to wake it up.\nAnyway, the Pokémon already looks like a bamboo plant so it doesn't seem too out of place with the forest environment."5\tg[Owen]Wow, \PN!\NHave you got your badge yet?"7\tg[Owen]Agh, what a pain.\nBut I'm happy for you!"?\tg[Simon]\wtnp[]Hello, \PN.\NAre you free now\..\..\..\.?"S\tg[Owen]Well, if it isn't Professor Simon! \nHeeeeeello, Professor Siiiiimon!".\tg[Simon]Tch.\nWrong time again\..\..\.."^\tg[Simon]Bah, never mind.\nFirst of all, tell me what happened at the end in the forest."\..\..\..\n\..\..\.."7\tg[Owen]Really!?\nMetis Corp. was in the forest!?"t\tg[Owen]And they were going after a Celesteela, but in the end they couldn't take it?\nWhy would they want it?"-\tg[Simon]Hmm\..\..\..\nI have a theory."�\tg[Simon]If their goal is to have everyone use the System, they would need to maintain a server capable of supporting many connections."�\tg[Simon]In the case of the \PN System, I can manage it just from the Academy without much problem \..\..\..\nBut they would require a lot of power."�\tg[Simon]Celesteela is a Pokémon capable of creating and storing large amounts of energy within its body.\nIt would also explain why they were after the Power Plant's energy."e\tg[Simon]That Teresa is tough as hell.\nI'm surprised you were able to win a match against her."�\tg[Simon]I guess the next step would be to ask Jeremiah for explanations, and what the former Champion have to do with all this. \nIt's getting more and more suspicious."�\tg[Simon]Oh, and what I wanted to tell you about! \nI guess you noticed when you defeated Teresa, but the System causes interference with the Metis Corp. system after the fights."�\tg[Simon]They are temporary eff