acks last, but does not miss."wThrows the target into the air and causes another Pokémon to come out. If it is a wild Pokémon, the battle ends."CAttacks the target with a shock wave and can even paralyze it."8A fast foot attack that reduces the target's speed."PAttack that produces double damage if the user is wounded in the same turn."@A fast, roundhouse kick. It can also knock the target back."QInflicts great damage to sleeping targets. However, slaps also wake them up."/Delivers a cutting blow. Usually critical."4A punch that is thrown quickly to strike first."OAttacks with punches that can break rocks. Can lower the target's Defense."ADelivers a withering blow. Always results in a critical hit."aSwing your fists and release a vacuum wave against the target. This move always comes first."A double kick. Hit twice.";Direct thrusts that strike two to five times in a row."<Kicks up to three times in a row and harder and harder."*Returns a physical blow in duplicate."\The user sacrifices himself causing damage to the target equivalent to his own lost HP."ALow kick. The heavier the target, the more damage it causes."GDesperate attack that causes more damage the less HP the user has."\Gravity knocks the target down. As many HP will be subtracted as the aggressor's level."9Strengthens the body to increase Attack and Defense."8Stops all attacks, but may fail if used repeatedly."\Protects the entire team from attacks that come before it. May fail if used repeatedly."cHits the target with a V of flames. Lowers the Defense, Special Defense and Speed of the user."=Explosion of fire. The attacker must rest the next turn."`Explosive fury. The lower the number of HP of the user, the less damage the attack will do."NA full-fledged attack that greatly lowers the Special Attack of the user."`Attacks with a beautiful but powerful blue flame that surrounds the target. It can burn it."@Intense flame that scorches everything and can cause burns."_The Pokémon is covered in flames and c