s himself at the opponent with great speed."aProtects the allied team from any move, except status attacks. Only works on the first turn."tCauses damage. To be performed, the user must have consumed a berry, either equipped or by pecking or stinging."Increases the attack and special attack by one level for each plant-type Pokémon in combat that is in contact with the ground."bCauses opposing Pokémon, when entering a battle, to have their speed decreased by one level."mCauses damage. If the opponent is weakened with this move, the user's attack is increased by two levels."UThe user disappears in the darkness for one turn. In the second turn he attacks."=Adds the ghost type to the original types of the target."]It is a sound move that lowers the target's attack and special attack by one level each."^Transforms normal type movements into electric ones during that turn. It has +1 priority."]Causes damage and the user recovers 50% of the HP removed by the movement to the target."WThe user casts a forest curse on the opponent, transforming him into a plant type.".It attacks with a great storm of flowers."iCauses damage and has a 10% chance of freezing the target. It is super effective against Water type."�Causes damage and has no side effects. This attack never misses, ignoring changes in the user's accuracy and the target's evasion."WThe user lowers the target's Attack and Special Attack, then swaps with a partner.";Completely reverses changes in target characteristics."]Causes damage and the user recovers 75% of the HP removed by the movement to the target."]It is a high priority move (+3) that protects the user and his allies from status moves."DIncreases the defense of all plant-type Pokémon in the battle."It covers the combat terrain with grass for five turns, recovers 1/16 of the maximum HP and boosts plant-like movements by 50%."bCovers the combat terrain with fog for five turns. Pokémon are not affected by stat changes."yIf used before the target, electrifica